---
import CompareLayout from "../../layouts/CompareLayout.astro";
import { deployRisk } from "../../data/demo-answers.ts";
import { SFI, VERIFIED } from "../../data/compare.ts";
---

<CompareLayout
  name="Salesforce’s MCP servers"
  title="sf-intelligence vs Salesforce DX MCP and Hosted MCP"
  description="Salesforce's MCP servers act on your org: records, deploys, tests. sf-intelligence explains it offline. What each does, DX MCP's end of life, when to use both."
  path="/compare/salesforce-dx-mcp"
  heading="sf-intelligence vs Salesforce’s MCP servers"
  lede="Salesforce’s own MCP servers let an AI assistant work with your org: query records, deploy, run tests. sf-intelligence answers questions about how the org is built, offline and read-only. They do different jobs, and many people run both."
  short="Use Salesforce’s servers to act: query and update records under your login (Hosted MCP), or deploy, retrieve and run tests from a project (the DX MCP server, which Salesforce says reaches end of life on November 2, 2026). Use sf-intelligence to understand: what depends on a field, what runs on save, who can edit what, whether a release is risky. It never writes to the org."
  rows={[
    { label: "Job", sfi: "Explain the org: dependencies, automation, access, deployment risk", them: "Act on the org: records and SOQL (Hosted MCP); metadata, deploys, tests and scratch orgs (DX MCP)" },
    { label: "Writes to the org", sfi: SFI.writes, them: "Yes, where enabled. Hosted MCP offers a read-only records server alongside create, update and delete servers; DX MCP can deploy metadata" },
    { label: "Where it runs", sfi: "On your computer, from a metadata snapshot. Works offline", them: "Hosted MCP runs in Salesforce. DX MCP runs locally and calls the org live" },
    { label: "Dependency and impact answers", sfi: "The main job: what depends on what, and what breaks", them: "Not their documented focus" },
    { label: "Price", sfi: SFI.price, them: "DX MCP is free and open source. For Hosted MCP edition and licence terms, check Salesforce’s documentation" },
    { label: "Status", sfi: "Actively developed", them: "Salesforce says the DX local MCP server reaches end of life on November 2, 2026, and points to skills instead" },
  ]}
  chooseSfi={[
    "To know <strong>what breaks</strong> before you delete a field, turn off a flow or deploy",
    "To find out <strong>why a user can’t see</strong> a record, or who can edit a field",
    "To learn an org you didn’t build, or document it",
    "<strong>No write access</strong> at all, and answers that work offline",
  ]}
  chooseThem={[
    "To <strong>query or change records</strong> from your assistant, under your Salesforce login",
    "To <strong>deploy, retrieve and run tests</strong> from an AI workflow",
    "A first-party tool inside Salesforce’s own trust boundary",
  ]}
  notSfi={[
    "You want the assistant to change records, metadata or settings. sf-intelligence can’t",
    "You need live record data as the main answer. The optional live mode reads capped counts and samples, but it isn’t a query tool",
  ]}
  example={deployRisk}
  exampleIntro="The kind of question sf-intelligence is for: a release reviewed before it is deployed, on Verdant, the demo org. Deploy it with whatever tool you already use."
  sources={[
    { label: "salesforcecli/mcp README (end-of-life notice, toolsets)", href: "https://github.com/salesforcecli/mcp" },
    { label: "forcedotcom/mcp issue 46: End of Life, November 2nd, 2026", href: "https://github.com/forcedotcom/mcp/issues/46" },
    { label: "Salesforce Hosted MCP Servers documentation", href: "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/hosted-mcp-servers/guide" },
  ]}
  verified={VERIFIED}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: "Can sf-intelligence replace Salesforce’s MCP servers?",
      a: "No. They do different jobs. Salesforce’s servers act on the org; sf-intelligence explains it and never changes anything. If you need both, register both in the same assistant. They don’t conflict.",
    },
    {
      q: "Is the Salesforce DX MCP server being retired?",
      a: "Salesforce’s notice says the DX local MCP server (@salesforce/mcp) reaches end of life on November 2, 2026: no further releases, the repositories archived, and the npm package marked deprecated but still installable. It points users to skills in the forcedotcom/sf-skills repository. sf-intelligence is a separate, independent project and isn’t affected.",
    },
    {
      q: "Do Salesforce’s servers answer “what breaks if I delete this field?”",
      a: "Their documentation focuses on records, queries, metadata deploys and tests, not on tracing dependencies across flows, Apex, formulas and permissions. That tracing is what sf-intelligence is built for.",
    },
  ]}
  related={[{ href: "/mcp", label: "What is a Salesforce MCP server?" }, { href: "/agent-skills", label: "Agent skills and MCP tools" }]}
>
  <h2>Two layers, both useful</h2>
  <p>A common setup: ask sf-intelligence what a change will break, fix what it names, then use a Salesforce server (or your usual deployment tool) to make the change. The first tool can’t write anything; the second is the one you trust with write access.</p>
</CompareLayout>
